window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>The North American Pack was always meant to be Ember's birthright, but she grew up far away from shifter culture in a sanctuary city for monsters.</b></p> <p>Her wolf yearns to scout pack lands and socialize with other wolves, but Ember understands the risks, especially considering female shifters are nearly endangered nowadays.</p> <p>So, she keeps her distance, even if she has to fight her wolf at every turn...</p> <p>And that works until Ember's team is called in on a mysterious case for the paranormal council. Their suspect has ties to the North American Pack, and Ember's wolf sees it as a perfect excuse to snoop around the pack lands.</p> <p>Only big things are happening in the supernatural world, and what happens next, none of them could have guessed.</p> <p>With her newly claimed mates at her back, will she be able to fix the injustices of the past? Or will everything unravel as quickly as it came together?</p> <p>Ember's Claim <i>is a standalone with no cliffhanger set in the same world as the A Monstrous World series. You don't need to have listened to those books to enjoy Ember's book.</i></p>"; 
